NAME
    finder - the desktop's file browser (the video card V4)

SYNOPSIS
    finder [dir]

DESCRIPTION
    Shows the folder dir (default /) in a window on the graphics
    screen. A row is a file: its name, its size (dir for a folder)
    and what it is - folder, program, script (.sh) or file.

    Press on a row to select it, press on it again to open it (or
    Enter, or Open in the menu bar). A folder is listed in the
    window; a program or a script runs, and another file opens in
    write, the editor. When a program ends, a key brings the finder
    back in the same folder (after write it comes back at once). Up in the menu bar (or Backspace, or the row ..)
    goes to the folder above; the arrow keys move the selection;
    Quit (or q) ends the finder.

    The window can be dragged by its title bar (an outline follows
    the mouse).

NOTES
    Needs the video card V4 and /lib/wmk, the window kernel (loaded
    again when a program has overwritten it). A program is run by
    the script /finder.sh, which the finder writes: the program,
    then finder -w (wait for a key, then the desktop). A program
    that ends with an error stops the script: type finder again.
    Written 2026-11-20 after the P8X's finder (os/lib_wm.c).
